EGL_ANGLE_window_fixed_size on the Metal backend (ADR-0029, decision 8).

Why: Android apps choose their buffer size with ANativeWindow_setBuffersGeometry, and SurfaceFlinger
scales the buffers onto the window. On Metal, WindowSurfaceMtl sets the CAMetalLayer's drawableSize to
the layer's bounds times its scale at every frame, so such a size cannot be kept. With
EGL_FIXED_SIZE_ANGLE the drawable keeps the surface's fixed size, eglSurfaceAttrib(EGL_WIDTH/EGL_HEIGHT)
changes it from the next drawable on (ANGLE's front end already validates both), and Core Animation
scales it onto the layer. DisplayMtl announces the extension.
Upstream: could go upstream; the extension exists for other backends.
Remove: when upstream implements EGL_ANGLE_window_fixed_size for Metal.

